From b4af23058b3665404c0aae2602da86a5d78d12cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Scope analysis/history/investigations to login; add-on
 magic-link handoff

Rebuilt against the real current main (the earlier version of this
work was built on a stale clone, 13 commits behind, and its patches
didn't apply). The teammate auth-flow commit (d6b4fbb) built the
login UI (profile menu, /auth/me, /auth/logout) but never actually
scoped /analyze, /history, or /investigation/<id> to the session --
they still trusted a client-supplied user_id, and the frontend still
fell back to demo@gmail.com whenever no one was logged in.

- login_required / identity_required (api.py): /history and
  /investigation/<id> require the website session; /analyze accepts
  either the session OR an X-API-Key + body user_id pair (the add-ins'
  channel -- trusted only because the key is a secret only our own
  add-ins hold, and that user_id comes from the mail platform's own
  verified identity, never a browser user).
- /investigation/<id> now checks row ownership, 404s (not 403) if a
  valid id belongs to someone else.
- CORS/redirects now use FRONTEND_URL instead of a hardcoded
  http://127.0.0.1:5173; SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE/SECURE toggle by
  FLASK_ENV=production for cross-origin cookies in deployment.
- google_callback and the new /auth/addon-session both call
  get_or_create_user so Neon's users table is populated at login time.
- /auth/addon-session: verifies a short-lived signed token (minted by
  /analyze for an add-in-sourced call) and sets the same session
  cookie Google OAuth would -- lets "VIEW FULL INVESTIGATION" in the
  Gmail add-on land already logged into that mailbox's account, with
  History showing that account's real past investigations immediately.
- Frontend: api.js sends credentials:"include" and exposes
  getCurrentUser()/logoutUrl(); app.jsx now calls those instead of a
  hardcoded 127.0.0.1:5001, drops every demo@gmail.com fallback, and
  routes 401s to the login view. LoginPage.jsx's Google-login link
  uses the configured API base URL instead of localhost.
- GmailEmailAnalyzer.gs's "VIEW FULL INVESTIGATION" button uses
  report_url when /analyze returns one.

Note: outlook-addon/ was found deleted from main by an unrelated
commit (5c545fc, "Updated ML model and feature selection") -- left
untouched this pass per instruction; needs a decision on whether that
deletion was intentional before any Outlook work resumes.
